    2. Pick background color from {1,2,3,5,6,7,8,9}
    3. Choose number of markers N in [3,6]
    4. Pick N-1 distinct arm colors from remaining non-bg, non-yellow, non-black palette; designate one as the answer (will appear twice), giving N arm assignments total
    5. Fill grid with background color
    6. Place N marker centers with Chebyshev distance >=5 between any pair and >=1 from edges; write yellow center + 4 arm pixels
    7. Scatter noise: fill 24-34% of non-marker cells with mostly black pixels (70%+ black, rest sampled from arm colors); prefer clustered placement via random walk or dilation
